Market Challenges
Maintaining consistent inhibitor performance during large-scale peptide production remains a technical challenge. Reaction conditions, amino-acid sequences, activation times, and reagent quality can influence racemization outcomes. Manufacturers must validate the effectiveness of selected additives across different synthesis processes.

Integration into established production workflows can also require changes to reaction monitoring, purification, and analytical testing. These requirements may extend development timelines and increase process qualification costs.

Market Restraints
Safety concerns associated with certain benzotriazole-based reagents can restrict adoption and encourage manufacturers to evaluate alternative chemistries. Handling, storage, and disposal requirements may add operational complexity.

High-purity specialty reagents can also increase production expenses, particularly for smaller biotechnology companies and research organizations. Alternative coupling chemistries and process redesign may reduce reliance on particular inhibitor categories, creating additional competitive pressure.

